WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.480
On November 18th, 1928, Mickey Mouse was
introduced to the world in the film

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.740
Steamboat Willie. But this may be one of
the last birthdays Mickey celebrates as

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.430
the intellectual property of Disney.
Copyrights for the popular character are

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.830
set to expire on January 1st, 2024. Mickey
might have become public property sooner

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.150
except that each time the copyright on
Steamboat Willie was set to lapse, Disney

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.920
and others pushed Congress to lengthen
US copyright terms. By 1998, works of

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.910
corporate authorship were exclusive
company property for 95 years from

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.079
publication. But this time around, there
doesn't seem to be any serious effort to

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:44.520
extend Disney's copyright for several
reasons. First, each version of Mickey

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.390
Mouse has a separate copyright, so only
the Steamboat Willie version will enter

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:53.250
the public domain in 2024. Second, Disney
has clearly diversified its stable of

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.570
copyrighted characters. Third, copyright
activists have out-organized Hollywood.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.320
And fourth, it's unlikely the public
would accept a copyright extension

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.660
beyond 95 years. So enjoy your day Mickey, because soon you will belong to your adoring public.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.420
What do you think? Will
Disney let its copyrights on Mickey

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:15.659
expire? Let us know in our poll. Also, let
us know what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:20.280
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
